# 19. False Positive

A **false positive** occurs when the tool reports something suspicious when the file is actually legitimate.

Example:

```text
Legitimate administration tool
        ↓
Contains "powershell"
        ↓
Scanner flags it
        ↓
False Positive
```

Therefore:

> Detection results require analyst validation.

---

# 20. False Negative

A **false negative** occurs when malicious software is not detected.

Example:

```text
Obfuscated malware
       ↓
No obvious strings
       ↓
Scanner reports LOW
       ↓
Malware was missed
```

Therefore:

> A LOW score does not guarantee safety.

